From: AlSukkar <dev@example.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] correct: revert broken security bumps, keep working Pkcs override

The previous patch (security-and-lockfix.patch) bumped several packages
to versions that don't exist on nuget.org or are themselves still
vulnerable, breaking restore:

  error NU1102: Unable to find package SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green
                with version (>= 2.1.14) [nearest: 2.1.11]
  warning NU1603: Tmds.DBus 0.21.3 not found, resolved 0.22.0 instead
                  (and 0.22.0 is STILL vulnerable per GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9)
  warning NU1903: System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.18 is vulnerable
                  to 3 newer advisories (GHSA-7hqp, GHSA-c399, GHSA-r955)

Mistakes and what we now know:

1. Tmds.DBus: the GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9 advisory lists 0.21.3 as a
   patched version, but that's only for the Tmds.DBus.Protocol package
   (which GalaxyBudsClient.Platform.Linux already uses correctly).
   For Tmds.DBus itself, the only patched version is 0.92.0 - a
   major API rewrite that would break compilation.
   => Revert to 0.21.2 and accept the warning. Android APK does not
      use D-Bus at runtime (Linux desktop only).

2. SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green / .lib.e_sqlite3.android: 2.1.14 does
   not exist on nuget.org. The latest available is 2.1.11, which is
   itself vulnerable (GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q). No patched version has
   been published yet.
   => Remove the explicit references. The transitive 2.1.11 will be
      used (as before). Warning remains until upstream ships a fix.

3. System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.18 was the patch for
   GHSA-23rf-6693-g89p, but three newer advisories (GHSA-7hqp,
   GHSA-c399, GHSA-r955) affect ALL 9.0.x versions. No 9.0.x fix
   exists yet - the patched versions are on 10.0.x (10.0.10+).
   => Remove the override; transitive 9.0.0 comes back. Same set of
      advisories either way; nothing actually got worse.

4. System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 9.0.21 - this one is CORRECT
   and actually closes GHSA-846f-f764-76mx (high) and
   GHSA-2fmv-rv2c-59x7 (moderate). Keep it.

5. GalaxyBudsClient.Generators.csproj <GenerateDependencyFile>false
   is unchanged - that fix was correct and the MSB4018 IOException
   has not recurred.

Net result: build unblocks, Pkcs is patched, Tmds.DBus and
SQLitePCLRaw warnings remain until upstream publishes fixes.

---
 GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj         | 17 +++++++++--------
 ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj       |  2 +-
 ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj |  2 +-
 3 files changed, 11 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj b/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
index e53aa25..05f7532 100644
--- a/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
+++ b/GalaxyBudsClient/GalaxyBudsClient.csproj
@@ -128,16 +128,17 @@
         <PackageReference Include="Serilog.Sinks.Trace" Version="4.0.0" />
         <!-- Workaround: force include SkiaSharp 3.x libraries for Linux; this is already implicitly the case for other platforms -->
         <PackageReference Include="SkiaSharp.NativeAssets.Linux" Version="3.119.1" />
-        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.3" />
+        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.2" />
 
-        <!-- Security overrides: force patched versions of transitive deps
-             pulled in via EF Core 10.0.3 / Microsoft.AspNet.WebApi.Client 6.0.0.
-             NuGet picks the lowest satisfying version, so explicit refs are
-             required to lift these above the vulnerable floor. -->
-        <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.bundle_green" Version="2.1.14" />
-        <PackageReference Include="SQLitePCLRaw.lib.e_sqlite3.android" Version="2.1.14" />
+        <!-- Security override: Tmds.DBus 0.21.2 has GHSA-xrw6-gwf8-vvr9 but
+             the only patched version is 0.92.0 (major API change). Android
+             build doesn't use D-Bus at runtime, so accept the warning.
+             SQLitePCLRaw 2.1.11 has GHSA-2m69-gcr7-jv3q but 2.1.11 is the
+             LATEST version on nuget.org - no patched version exists yet.
+             System.Security.Cryptography.Xml 9.0.x is vulnerable across all
+             9.0.x versions per newer advisories; no fix available on 9.0.x.
+             Only Pkcs has a real fix available; lift it explicitly. -->
         <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs" Version="9.0.21" />
-        <PackageReference Include="System.Security.Cryptography.Xml" Version="9.0.18" />
     </ItemGroup>
 
 
diff --git a/ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj b/ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj
index f108fe9..cb7dd17 100644
--- a/ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj
+++ b/ThePBone.BlueZNet/ThePBone.BlueZNet.csproj
@@ -17,6 +17,6 @@
 
     <ItemGroup>
         <PackageReference Include="Serilog" Version="4.3.0" />
-        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.3" />
+        <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.2" />
     </ItemGroup>
 </Project>
diff --git a/ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj b/ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj
index ca4513a..9179bf8 100644
--- a/ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj
+++ b/ThePBone.MprisClient/ThePBone.MprisClient.csproj
@@ -11,6 +11,6 @@
     
     <ItemGroup>
       <PackageReference Include="Serilog" Version="4.3.0" />
-      <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.3" />
+      <PackageReference Include="Tmds.DBus" Version="0.21.2" />
     </ItemGroup>
 </Project>
